@copilot Update this PR directly with one narrowly scoped correction to the new tools/runner/tests/test_scenario_matrix.py tests. The automatic four-way sharding behavior and the current PR scope should remain unchanged.

The delivered test module invokes subprocess.run and subprocess.check_output without Windows no-window creation flags, including the standalone Python CLI and tracked-files tests that run on Windows. Repository instructions require every Python subprocess capable of starting a console program on Windows to use CREATE_NO_WINDOW, centralize that launch behavior, and cover it with regression tests. The Linux-only integration test also has subprocess launches and should use the same helper consistently.

Reuse an appropriate existing helper if available, or add a small test-local helper that applies subprocess.CREATE_NO_WINDOW on Windows and zero creation flags elsewhere, preserving each call's current capture, input, check, cwd, and environment behavior. Route every subprocess launch introduced by this test module through that helper. Add focused regression coverage of the Windows and non-Windows launch options without actually opening a console. Run the focused scenario-matrix tests and relevant lint/type checks. Do not expand into unrelated test cleanup, production-runner changes, or other workflow changes.

@copilot Fix the lint regression from commit 86d1a65 directly on this PR. In tools/runner/tests/test_scenario_matrix.py:27, the new run_subprocess helper's input parameter triggers Ruff A002, "Function argument `input` is shadowing a Python builtin". The failed job is https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-conformance/actions/runs/40133975334/job/120994371954?pr=383 and used Ruff 0.17.2.

Rename the helper parameter to a non-builtin name such as input_text and update every helper call site, including the platform regression test. Continue forwarding its value through subprocess.run(input=...), and keep the mock assertion checking the actual subprocess keyword "input". Preserve the existing subprocess options, Windows CREATE_NO_WINDOW behavior, all remaining tests, and sharding behavior. Do not suppress A002 or weaken lint configuration. Leave production code and workflows unchanged.

Run Ruff on the changed test file using the repository configuration and the focused scenario-matrix tests. If required validation tools are missing, install the relevant existing development dependencies rather than relying on syntax-only checks; report any genuine installation or validation blocker accurately. Keep this follow-up limited to this regression and do not create another PR.
